  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 232 AM EDT Mon Aug 10 2026\n\nEarly morning GOES WV imagery indicates a broad troughing pattern \nacross central and eastern Canada and ridging centered over the Four \nCorners, while in between, we are under mainly zonal flow over the \nGreat Lakes. Apart from some patchy fog developing early this \nmorning, skies remain mostly clear with weak surface ridging over \nthe UP. Fog mixes out after sunrise, then expect mostly sunny skies \nfollowed by increasing clouds overnight into Tuesday. Temperatures \npeak in the 70s across most of the area, and in the lower 80s across \nthe south-central UP. Expect lows in the 50s by early Tuesday. \n\nThe rest of the week sees a slow trend to slightly cooler than \nnormal temps as highs trend toward upper 60s to mid 70s for the end \nof the work week with lows in the 40s to mid 50s. Shortwaves Tuesday \nand Wednesday yield chances for showers and storms (25-50% chance) \nwith plenty of timing/coverage uncertainty. Bulk shear will be \nstrong, but instability is not forecast to be very impressive so \nsevere weather is not expected at this time. Finally the broad \nCanadian troughing pattern breaks down late this week and stronger \nhigh pressure returns to the Great Lakes, favoring drier weather \ninto the weekend. PoPs return late Saturday into Sunday as ensembles \ntrack a low pressure system into the region.",
